meta {
  name: register
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/student/registration/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. Lowercased on save, and must not already exist -- including an
    // account created earlier by a guest checkout.
    "email": "nueva.estudiante@example.com",

    // Required, minimum 8 characters. Also run through Django's
    // AUTH_PASSWORD_VALIDATORS: not too similar to the email, not a common
    // password, not entirely numeric.
    "password1": "caminante2026",

    // Must match password1 exactly. Required.
    "password2": "caminante2026",

    // Required.
    "first_name": "Nueva",

    // Optional.
    "last_name": "Estudiante",

    // Optional.
    "country": "Spain",

    // Optional.
    "phone_number": "+34 600 123 456",

    // Optional IANA timezone, defaults to "America/Guayaquil" (the school's).
    // Everything in the portal is rendered in this zone. Unknown zone -> 400.
    "timezone": "Europe/Madrid",

    // Optional, defaults to "none". One of:
    // "none", "beginner", "intermediate", "upper_intermediate", "advanced".
    "current_spanish_level": "beginner"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  const response = res.getBody();

  // Only present when EMAIL_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED=False.
  if (response.access) {
    bru.setVar("accessTokenStudent", response.access);
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Creates a `User` (flagged `is_student`) **and** the matching `Student` profile
  in one call, so the account can use the portal immediately.

  The response depends on `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED`:

  - **True** -- 201 with `email_verification_required: true` and no tokens. A
    confirmation email goes out; the account cannot log in until the link is
    clicked (login returns 403). Continue with **verify email**.
  - **False** -- 201 with `access` / `refresh` / `role` / `profile`, exactly like
    a login. The address is marked verified on creation.

  `POST /rest-auth/registration/` is the same view under its legacy path. It used
  to be dj-rest-auth's default, which created a `User` with no `Student` profile
  and no `is_student` flag -- an account that could not use any portal endpoint.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "email_verification_required": true,
    "email": "nueva.estudiante@example.com",
    "message": "Almost there. Check your inbox and click the link to activate your account."
  }
}
